          {
            "id": 621,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-Ck89d6kV0oBzsQx3pyalXOLQgWe\">The process undergoes five stages, beginning with the initial mixing of water and milk, and concluding with the cooling of the final product at a specific temperature.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13888,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 622,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-QCeJdfGOzou3zuxzOA4lCnsBg2c\">The process begins when water and milk are combined in a mixing chamber, where a mixture is formed. This mixture then enters the first cooling process, where it is maintained at 5 degrees Celsius for two hours. Following this, the mixture moves to the fermentation phase, where salt is added, and the mixture is heated to 37 degrees Celsius for a period of six hours.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13888,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 623,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-JUFFd40tromWp1xwO4FlqFRVgsc\">In the latter stages of production, the mixture is heated to 100 degrees Celsius during an evaporation process that lasts eight hours, producing steam as a by-product. Finally, in the final cooling stage, the soft cheese is cooled to 5 degrees Celsius for eight hours, during which waste water is removed through a filtration system, resulting in the finished soft cheese product.</div>\n</div>",
